1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,220
The US Corn Belt just received a glowing report.

2
00:00:03,240 --> 00:00:03,780
3
00:00:03,800 --&gt; 00:00:09,050
A new study helps confirm that the Midwest is one of the most productive regions on Earth.

3
00:00:09,070 --> 00:00:09,580
5
00:00:09,600 --&gt; 00:00:14,630
The findings are based on a new way of estimating plant productivity from space.

4
00:00:14,650 --> 00:00:15,060
7
00:00:15,080 --&gt; 00:00:21,950
The method uses chlorophyll fluorescence data, which is a measurement of the amount of light a plant emits during photsynthesis.

5
00:00:21,970 --> 00:00:22,360
9
00:00:22,380 --&gt; 00:00:28,870
The light appears as a faint glow that's invisible to the naked eye, but can be detected by satellites.

6
00:00:28,890 --> 00:00:29,260
11
00:00:29,280 --&gt; 00:00:38,870
In 2013, a team of researchers led by NASA scientists demonstrated that plant fluorescence could be accurately mapped using satellite data.

7
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:39,300
13
00:00:39,320 --&gt; 00:00:46,580
Now, the measurements are being applied for the first time to assess the productivity of croplands around the world.

8
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:51,980
15
00:00:52,000 --&gt; 00:00:52,470